[ti:Wisdom Can't Be Taught]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:Sidd-hartha.text - Reawakened]

[00:04.54]Yeah... books keep talkin'... but the soul stay quiet
[00:17.58]Instrumental
[00:20.77]Sat with the wise ones, learned every verse by heart
[00:23.97]Breathed the sacred words till the pages fell apart
[00:26.48]Fasted till the bones showed, meditated till the mind went still
[00:29.73]But the final piece was missin', and the cup stayed unfilled
[00:32.43]They was pourin' ancient knowledge like rivers in my ears
[00:35.08]But the thirst stayed the same after all them years
[00:37.76]Heard enlightened voices, clear as crystal stream
[00:40.32]Yet the deepest secret stayed locked inside the dream
[00:42.87]Three years with the Samanas, ash and sun and stone
[00:45.32]Learned to be a heron, learned to be a bone
[00:47.96]Slipped into a jackal, rotted in the sand
[00:50.40]Came back every mornin' with the same empty hand
[00:53.17]Old man of the forest, sixty years of pain
[00:56.03]Never reached Nirvana, just a longer chain
[00:58.56]Govinda asked me, "brother, are we gettin' close?"
[01:00.86]I said we only learnin' tricks to fool ourselves the most
[01:04.01]Wisdom can't be taught (wisdom can't be taught)
[01:08.99]Can't be bought or caught, only earned in the dark
[01:14.33]Wisdom can't be taught (wisdom can't be taught)
[01:18.93]Only lived, only felt, every scar leaves a mark
[01:24.27]Walked the path of pain, then I walked the path of denial
[01:27.52]Chased the light in silence, mile after mile
[01:30.23]Then a rumor in the villages, a man in yellow robe
[01:32.94]Gotama the Awakened, peace in every step he strode
[01:35.93]Saw him in the grove, every gesture like a lake
[01:38.29]Not a single motion wasted, not a single move fake
[01:41.09]Govinda hit his knees, took the refuge, took the vow
[01:43.49]I bowed down to the Buddha, but I couldn't follow now
[01:46.36]Every holy teachin' felt like secondhand fire
[01:48.96]Real flame only burns when you walk through your own desire
[01:52.13]No teacher, no scripture, no sacred word could fill
[01:54.44]The quiet space inside me where the real answer's still
[01:56.94]Told him, "Your words is perfect, but the words ain't the way
[01:59.52]What you found beneath the tree, no sermon can convey"
[02:02.27]He just smiled and said, "Beware of bein' too clever, friend"
[02:05.28]And I left my only shadow standin' at the river's bend
[02:08.40]Wisdom can't be taught (wisdom can't be taught)
[02:12.84]Can't be bought or caught, only earned in the dark
[02:18.20]Wisdom can't be taught (wisdom can't be taught)
[02:22.97]Only lived, only felt, every scar leaves a mark
[02:29.17]Had to lose the map, had to burn the guide
[02:31.57]Had to let the self die just to see the other side
[02:34.37]The arrow flies forever, but the target is the bow
[02:37.13]Gotta kill the seeker just to let the seeker know
[02:39.50]Wisdom can't be taught (wisdom can't be taught)
[02:44.83]Can't be bought or caught, only earned in the dark
[02:50.20]Wisdom can't be taught (wisdom can't be taught)
[02:54.82]Only lived, only felt, every scar leaves a mark
[03:02.83]Books keep talkin'... but the soul stay quiet
[03:09.14]Wisdom can't be taught
[03:11.54]Only lived... only felt... only earned in the dark
[03:17.41]
